{"id":"CVE-2018-12029","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-06-17T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T08:24:03.642Z","description":"A race condition in the nginx module in Phusion Passenger 3.x through 5.x before 5.3.2 allows local escalation of privileges when a non-standard passenger_instance_registry_dir with insufficiently strict permissions is configured. Replacing a file with a symlink after the file was created, but before it was chowned, leads to the target of the link being chowned via the path. Targeting sensitive files such as root's crontab file allows privilege escalation.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://blog.phusion.nl/passenger-5-3-2","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201807-02","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201807-02"},{"url":"https://pulsesecurity.co.nz/advisories/phusion-passenger-priv-esc","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2018/06/msg00007.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20180627 [SECURITY] [DLA 1399-1] ruby-passenger security update"}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-16843","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2018-11-07T14:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T10:32:54.156Z","description":"nginx before versions 1.15.6 and 1.14.1 has a vulnerability in the implementation of HTTP/2 that can allow for excessive memory consumption. This issue affects nginx compiled with the ngx_http_v2_module (not compiled by default) if the 'http2' option of the 'listen' directive is used in a configuration file.","cwe":["CWE-400 CWE-400"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":5.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"[UNKNOWN]","product":"nginx","versions":["affected 1.15.6","affected 1.14.1"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4335","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4335"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3680","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3680"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3681","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3681"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/105868","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"105868"},{"url":"http://mailman.nginx.org/pipermail/nginx-announce/2018/000220.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1042038","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1042038"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2018-16843","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3653","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3653"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3812-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3812-1"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-09/msg00035.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:2120"},{"url":"https://support.apple.com/kb/HT212818","tags":["x_refsource